        "title": "Happened upon a festival and couldn't believe it!",
        "text": "What an experience, this is like nothing I've seen before.\nOur hotel tried to talk us out of going when we did due to it being busy with a festival. We were so glad we went any way, the area was decorated and there were people everywhere. \nSuch an interesting experience.\n\nA couple of tips - as a foreigner there will be a guide at the entry desk and they will most likely just start talking with you and giving you information. I'd recommend you agree on a price prior to continuing (we got to the end and weren't sure if the price was fair).\nAlong the way you will see the sadhu's (painted holy men), if you take a picture with them - they expect to be paid. Hopefully the money goes to the hospice like we were told. \nYou'll also come across people selling jewellery and trinkets, if you have no intention of buying anything don't give and ounce of hope - no means maybe - maybe means yes...\nSoak it up and enjoy the experience, note: it's a good idea to have a guide so they can inform you of where you are allowed and when it's appropriate to take photos to avoid offending.",
