      {
        "review_id": 638087483,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r638087483-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Humbling experience",
        "text": "I had the privilege of witnessing my first body being cremated in traditional Hindu fashion. The entry fee is steep for tourists at 1000nrp (Nepalese get in for free) but once in, there are guides wanting to show you around. We had this one bloke tell us the basics of cremation and the ceremonies around the passing of a family member. He later asked us if we would like to pay for a more in depth understanding of the temple and it's significance another 1000), but we declined. He was a certified guide but we just enjoy looking around. Witnessing the cremations was very heavy but if there's one thing I implore visitors to do, is to be discreet if you want to take photos. There were a few tourists who were getting amongst the ceremony trying to get a shot of those who have just lost a loved one, like it was a movie set or something. It was really disappointing that they had no respect for the people they were taking pictures of. I would hate having some tourists snapping away at a funeral I attended. So please be respectful and don't be trying to get the best close up of a lady's tears...",
