      {
        "review_id": 636824812,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r636824812-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "A very powerful place",
        "text": "There is something in the air in Pashpatinath. An aura of the ancient, timeless ceremonies focusing on the cremation of the dead occur on the ghats. We sit and watch. So does everyone else. It brings life and death instantly to our eyes, a powerful reminder of that which awaits us all, that which we often try not to focus on, that which we try to avoid. It's all there, the wooden funeral pyres, distraught relatives watching on all in a setting of chaotic beauty. \n Often missed a walk to the top of the hill is a must where hundreds of tiny temples inhabit tree lined paths scattered with bells and monkeys. The cafe up there does very good momos. \n\n  A trip to Kathmandu really is not complete without an afternoon in Pashpatinath. Take your time, sit and watch let's the atmosphere take you forward or back in time under the tropical sun. \n\n Beautiful ",
